Server bootstrap
ts
// src/server.ts
import express from "express";
import cors from "cors";
import api from "./api";
import { env } from "./config/env";
import { logger } from "./shared/logger";
import { AppError } from "./shared/errors";

const app = express();

app.use(cors());
app.use(express.json());

app.use("/api", api);

// Error handler
app.use(
  (
    err: any,
    req: express.Request,
    res: express.Response,
    next: express.NextFunction
  ) => {
    logger.error("Unhandled error", err);
    const status = err instanceof AppError ? err.statusCode : 500;
    res.status(status).json({ error: err.message || "Internal server error" });
  }
);

app.listen(env.port, () => {
  logger.info(`J-ROC backend running on port ${env.port}`);
});
How this maps to your operating model
“J-ROC, build me this app.”  
→ POST /api/missions/build  
→ OrchestratorService.createBuildMission()  
→ Mission + blueprint tasks + agent assignment + status IN_PROGRESS.

“J-ROC, what’s the status?”  
→ GET /api/missions/:id/status  
→ OrchestratorService.getMissionStatus()  
→ Summary + approvals + deploy readiness.

Swarm Agent System  
→ AgentService + TaskService.assignTask() + roles RESEARCH/PRODUCT/UI_UX/FRONTEND/BACKEND/DATABASE/QA.
